+// The free-speech voice (the player's pick, 2026-11-12: of six clips, the two copying people talking freely were "by far" the
+// closest to people heard in real life): Pocket TTS (Kyutai 2026, 100M parameters, the ONNX export KevinAHM/pocket-tts-onnx,
+// CC BY 4.0) speaks a said stretch in the voice of a real recording, a speaker of EARS talking freely (Richter et al. 2024;
+// data/ears-voices.ts), the one whose copied voice is nearest the speaker's own computed pitch, tract and age. The networks run
+// in the worker (voice-worker.ts); this file holds what they need around them: the text's tokens, the stretches the model
+// takes at once, the recording's samples at 24 kHz, the choice of recording.
+import { POCKET_PIECES } from './data/pocket-tokenizer.js';
+import { EARS_VOICES, EARS_MEDIANS } from './data/ears-voices.js';
+import { MEASURED } from './voice-sound.js';
+import { def, peek } from './constants.js';
